title: trash panel
tags: Panel Trash
kind: reference
aliases: restore empty
summary: Lists the repository's trash entries, newest first, to restore or delete them.

Open it with `panel:open here trash` (<<key "panel:open here trash" "t b">>). One
row per entry — name, size, age, reason, the path it was trashed from — newest
first.

* <<key "trash:restore" Enter>> — restore the selected entry to its original path, metarecords included ([[What restoring does]]). Not a button on the row, nor a double click: it writes to the disk, on a row clicked often ([[Opening a row]]).
* <<key "trash:delete" Delete>> — delete the selected entry permanently (confirmed).
* `trash:empty` — delete every entry permanently (confirmed).
* <<key "cursor:find self select" f>> — jump to an entry by name; each candidate shows the path it was trashed from, so two entries sharing a name are still told apart ([[Jumping to an entry]]).
* <<key "cursor:next self" "↓ or j">> / <<key "cursor:prev self" "↑ or k">>, <<key "cursor:first self" Home>> / <<key "cursor:last self" End>> — move the selection; <<key "view:refresh self" r>> — reload the entries.

Pruning by age or size is command-line only ([[Trash retention]]).
